            <ArticleTitle>P(URI)fying Novel Drivers of NASH and HCC: A Feedforward Loop of IL17A via White Adipose Tissue.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-17</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1535-6108(16)30270-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ccell.2016.06.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>How obesity and metabolic syndrome trigger non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH) and hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) remains elusive. In this issue, Gomes and colleagues describe that nutrient surplus induces hepatic URI expression, triggering genotoxicity and IL17A expression, thus leading to insulin resistance, NASH, and HCC. IL17A signaling blockers might become a readily translatable therapy.</AbstractText>
